{"3985160": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Last Manifest", "steam_appid": 3985160, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/b764e553e6dc71c6d03319602dea3630.avif?t=1767468412\" width=1560 height=730 /></span>The Last Manifest is a cooperative horror game about a space crew trapped inside a ship that refuses to let them go.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are officers sent to investigate cargo disappearances. But instead of cargo, you find failing systems, endless malfunctions, and the only document left behind by the former crew: the manifest.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c6ec79202c665bb99f3b913e3af93380.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/6e90e5530039e1c59c295f49ebdd16cb.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/6e90e5530039e1c59c295f49ebdd16cb.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/6e90e5530039e1c59c295f49ebdd16cb.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>Repair. Adapt. Survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your mission is to bring the ship back to life and find a way home. Every mechanism can fail, every compartment can become a trap.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/93cfc1391261c5d2a33a2955febe7062.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c7211cce97d9a2508f14f7071baca1fe.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c7211cce97d9a2508f14f7071baca1fe.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c7211cce97d9a2508f14f7071baca1fe.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>The ship is not on your side.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It changes with you. Doors close on their own, routes vanish, corridors stretch. Every attempt at repair only raises new questions.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/609583ef3e2b185d42fb7021cd07a294.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/cb29b6602d9e4f97e17956bb9758b4b4.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/cb29b6602d9e4f97e17956bb9758b4b4.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/cb29b6602d9e4f97e17956bb9758b4b4.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>You hear voices. Not all of them are yours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The intercom transmits fragments of phrases, system logs write themselves. Sometimes it feels like you’re fixing what you’ve already fixed. Sometimes — like someone else has done it before you.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/04c20b1264998cd1c6af9bed67d7ef62.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/071e9fbdd95dbbc40a54b5e1d13e4ee1.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/071e9fbdd95dbbc40a54b5e1d13e4ee1.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/071e9fbdd95dbbc40a54b5e1d13e4ee1.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>Fun on the edge of panic. <br> This is a story of repairs spiraling into chaos. One holds a flashlight, another tries to open a panel, the third accidentally sets off the alarm. You laugh as the corridors rumble — until the laughter dies, and everyone listens to the silence again. <br> <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/a5f5482271e08c7606d492b4f73b1a72.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/e92748f9a78bb0fc0194532e08ab5c71.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/e92748f9a78bb0fc0194532e08ab5c71.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/e92748f9a78bb0fc0194532e08ab5c71.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>You are not alone. <br><br>There are those who have long settled in these dead compartments. They move behind bulkheads, whisper from the vents, appear in reflections. They can’t really be called “crew.” They’re more like a part of the ship itself. And they are not happy to see new guests. <br> <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/faae824d7a189c67d594ba7ecf8afd60.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/561e1fa399df087178c1f601b87a2d5b.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/561e1fa399df087178c1f601b87a2d5b.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/561e1fa399df087178c1f601b87a2d5b.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>The Last Manifest is a horror story about those who were meant to leave, but never could.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And the further you go, the stronger the feeling grows that the missing ones… are you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The manifest lists dates and surnames. They look familiar.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As if your escape has already failed once before.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And now the ship only invites you to repeat this path — again and again.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/b764e553e6dc71c6d03319602dea3630.avif?t=1767468412\" width=1560 height=730 /></span>The Last Manifest is a cooperative horror game about a space crew trapped inside a ship that refuses to let them go.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are officers sent to investigate cargo disappearances. But instead of cargo, you find failing systems, endless malfunctions, and the only document left behind by the former crew: the manifest.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c6ec79202c665bb99f3b913e3af93380.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/6e90e5530039e1c59c295f49ebdd16cb.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/6e90e5530039e1c59c295f49ebdd16cb.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/6e90e5530039e1c59c295f49ebdd16cb.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>Repair. Adapt. Survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your mission is to bring the ship back to life and find a way home. Every mechanism can fail, every compartment can become a trap.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/93cfc1391261c5d2a33a2955febe7062.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c7211cce97d9a2508f14f7071baca1fe.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c7211cce97d9a2508f14f7071baca1fe.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/c7211cce97d9a2508f14f7071baca1fe.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>The ship is not on your side.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It changes with you. Doors close on their own, routes vanish, corridors stretch. Every attempt at repair only raises new questions.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/609583ef3e2b185d42fb7021cd07a294.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/cb29b6602d9e4f97e17956bb9758b4b4.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/cb29b6602d9e4f97e17956bb9758b4b4.webm?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/cb29b6602d9e4f97e17956bb9758b4b4.mp4?t=1767468412\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>You hear voices. Not all of them are yours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The intercom transmits fragments of phrases, system logs write themselves. Sometimes it feels like you’re fixing what you’ve already fixed. Sometimes — like someone else has done it before you.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/04c20b1264998cd1c6af9bed67d7ef62.avif?t=1767468412\" width=750 height=100 /></span><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3985160/extras/071e9fbdd95dbbc40a54b5e1d13e4ee1.poster.avif?t=1767468412\" width=614 height=288 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/st